Purpose
-------
The preceding dual-site stride-512 pair first showed a different sampled
threshold predicate at global poll-hit ordinal 1,175,552. This diagnostic
replayed both source nonces and inputs with a dense inclusive poll-hit window
around that ordinal, preserving the entry stream. It checks actual poll
sequence positions within a call and corrects the interpretation of matching
global ordinals when earlier call lengths differ.

Configuration and command
-------------------------
Both direct runs use the exact nonce, inputs and Linux options from the
automatic source pair `stage5-s5-07-rdtsc-dual-site-stride512-n2-20261116-a`.
The poll RIP is 0xffffffff8271b34d, the entry RIP is 0xffffffff8271b31b, and
the dense selected-site window is inclusive global hit ordinals
1,150,000:1,200,000 with stride 1. The entry stream captures every hit.

Common command arguments:
```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --vmlinuz work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 \
  --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode --linux-norandmaps \
  --linux-no-randomize-kstack-offset \
  --execution-observations-rdtsc-rip 0xffffffff8271b34d \
  --execution-observations-rdtsc-stride 1 \
  --execution-observations-rdtsc-entry-rip 0xffffffff8271b31b \
  --execution-observations-rdtsc-window 1150000:1200000
```

Run 0001 adds `--nonce OD518e8a0fda5d3f4600000175200000000`, output
`work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-rdtsc-window-replay-20261116-a/run-0001.json`, and
`--execution-observations-out` to the correspondingly named run-0001 sidecar.
Run 0002 uses nonce `OD518e8a2228ca02d300000175200000001` and run-0002 output
and sidecar paths.

Both direct replays loaded Linux and stopped at `retired=2,999,999,998` with
`budget_exhausted`. For each nonce, the complete stop object, UART bytes and
full entry sample stream exactly match that nonce's automatic source run.
Each replay also matches all 97 source stride-512 poll samples whose global
ordinals fall inside the dense window. This establishes replay identity for
these inputs on this host/build; it does not prove nonce causality or benignity.

Window capture and join validation
---------------------------------
Both sidecars use schema v9 and record window `{first_hit: 1150000,
last_hit: 1200000}`. Each has exactly 50,001 retained poll samples, zero poll
omissions, and a global selected-site hit total beyond the end of the window.
Run 0001 has 43,871/43,871 entry hits/samples; run 0002 has 43,868/43,868;
both entry streams have zero omissions. Sidecars are 26,470,884 and
26,470,150 bytes.

Every dense poll sample joins uniquely to one entry sample by exact
`poll.start_tsc == entry.observed_tsc`, then matching requested cycles, RBP,
and RSP: 50,001 joins per replay, with zero unmatched, ambiguous, or
context-mismatched records.

Per-call poll sequence comparison
---------------------------------
The 53 shared entry ordinals represented in the window include 51 complete
interior calls, identified by contiguous global poll ordinals, first/last hits
strictly within the window, and a final threshold-true sample. Two window-edge
calls may be partial and are excluded from exact count claims. Across the 51
complete calls, 49,710 local poll positions can be paired by entry ordinal
and read index; nine predicates `elapsed_cycles >= requested_cycles` differ
at the same local poll position. The first is entry ordinal 10,196, poll read
975: run 0001 has elapsed
`0xf3be0` (false) and continues through read 977, where it reaches `0xf43d0`
(true); run 0002 has elapsed `0xf4452` (true) at read 975 and exits that
poll sequence there. The full call has 977 reads in run 0001 and 975 in run
0002. Window-edge calls may be partial; no count is claimed for those.

The previously highlighted entry ordinal 10,207 has 974 poll reads in both
runs. Both are false through local read 973 and true at read 974, with no
predicate difference at any matching local poll position. Its global poll
ordinal range is 1,174,582–1,175,555 in run 0001 and
1,174,579–1,175,552 in run 0002. Therefore global ordinal 1,175,552 refers
to local read 971 in run 0001 (`0xf3631`, false) but local read 974 in run
0002 (`0xf4219`, true). The earlier sparse comparison paired the same global
ordinal across the runs, which selected different poll iterations because
prior calls had accumulated a three-hit offset. That sparse difference does
not indicate a different exit iteration for call 10,207.

The dense evidence locates an earlier same-local-position threshold
difference at call 10,196 but does not explain the complete machine/UART
variation, identify the first unsampled divergence over the whole guest run,
or establish benignity. The overall automatic comparator remains false;
these direct replays are diagnostic and are not acceptance evidence.

